  "note": {
    "status": "draft",
    "text": "To read a big number, split the digits into groups of three from the right: units, thousands, millions. So 2405012 is written 2 405 012.\n\nRead each group, then say its name:\n2 405 012 → two million four hundred and five thousand and twelve.\n\nWe say 'and' after hundred: 305 is three hundred and five. Numbers from 21 to 99 take a hyphen: forty-five.\n\nTo write words in figures, fill every place. If a place is empty, write 0:\n• three thousand and five → 3005\n• forty thousand three hundred and seven → 40 307\nA common mistake is to leave out the zeros and write 35 or 437.\n\nOn a receipt, an amount is often written in words and in figures, so that nobody can change it.",
    "checks": [
      "words(2405012) == 'two million four hundred and five thousand and twelve'",
      "words(305) == 'three hundred and five'",
      "words(45) == 'forty-five'",
      "words(3005) == 'three thousand and five'",
      "words(40307) == 'forty thousand three hundred and seven'",
      "stripZeros(3005) == 35",
      "stripZeros(40307) == 437"
    ]
  },
  "worked_example": {
    "status": "draft",
    "vars": {
      "n": 6070040,
      "m": {
        "expr": "idiv(n, 1000000)"
      },
      "t": {
        "expr": "idiv(n, 1000) % 1000"
      },
      "u": {
        "expr": "n % 1000"
      }
    },
    "problem": "Write in figures: {words(n)}.",
    "steps": [
      "Millions group: {words(m)} → {m}.",
      "Thousands group: {words(t)} → {t}. Every group after the first needs three digits: {pad(t, 3)}.",
      "Units group: {words(u)} → {u}, written with three digits: {pad(u, 3)}.",
      "Put the groups together: {m} {pad(t, 3)} {pad(u, 3)}."
    ],
    "answer": "{words(n)} = {n}",
    "checks": [
      "m * 1000000 + t * 1000 + u == n",
      "fromWords(words(n)) == n",
      "str(m) + pad(t, 3) + pad(u, 3) == str(n)"
    ]
  },
